WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.735
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.005 --> 00:06.006
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

3
00:06.089 --> 00:07.925
THERE IS NO RELATION TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

4
00:08.759 --> 00:11.011
[siren wailing]

5
00:59.768 --> 01:01.228
[♪ gentle music playing]

6
01:05.065 --> 01:07.067
[in Korean] Are you okay?

7
01:37.598 --> 01:38.599
Yeah.

8
01:40.934 --> 01:42.060
I'm fine.

9
02:00.996 --> 02:02.581
Oh, uh…

10
02:05.042 --> 02:06.251
Whoa!

11
02:09.338 --> 02:11.173
[♪ comical music playing]

12
02:16.928 --> 02:18.221
NEW JAPANESE FOR TOTAL BEGINNERS

13
02:18.305 --> 02:21.350
EPISODE 3

14
02:23.185 --> 02:25.896
[shower runs, stops]

15
02:26.980 --> 02:27.981
[sighs]

16
02:28.899 --> 02:31.318
[in English] Was it all right that I let him in?

17
02:31.401 --> 02:32.402
[door closes]

18
02:37.991 --> 02:40.494
-Uh… -Oh, uh…

19
02:41.203 --> 02:44.289
-Right here. Sofa. Uh-huh. Tonight. -Oh. Sofa. Sofa. [grunts]

20
02:44.373 --> 02:46.625
[in Korean] I can sleep here?

21
02:46.708 --> 02:48.543
-[in English] Okay, okay. [chuckles] -Yes, good night.

22
02:48.627 --> 02:49.628
Thank you.

23
02:51.672 --> 02:52.798
[in Korean] About that.

24
02:55.425 --> 02:56.426
Uh…

25
02:59.596 --> 03:02.015
That figurine.

26
03:02.974 --> 03:05.143
Mmm. That one…

27
03:05.227 --> 03:07.646
-[in English] Oh, this? -[in Korean] Yeah, um… Ah!

28
03:08.814 --> 03:10.440
-[in English] This? -[in Korean] Yeah.

29
03:11.108 --> 03:13.985
Do you like that character?

30
03:15.529 --> 03:16.697
[sighs]

31
03:16.780 --> 03:18.407
[in English] Uh, no, that's not why.

32
03:19.116 --> 03:20.909
I'm holding it for someone else.

33
03:26.415 --> 03:28.083
-[in Korean] Holding on to it? -Mm-hmm.

34
03:28.166 --> 03:31.503
[in English] Oh, the Korean guy I told you about earlier

35
03:31.586 --> 03:33.630
bought this as a souvenir for his son.

36
03:42.556 --> 03:44.766
[in Korean] Is there anything else you know about that man?

37
03:48.395 --> 03:50.147
[in English] Um, I was very little…

38
03:53.650 --> 03:54.693
Ah…

39
03:55.360 --> 03:57.863
I do have some of Mr. Gyeongsu's belongings.

40
04:03.702 --> 04:06.413
My grandpa put everything in this suitcase.

41
04:07.539 --> 04:11.168
We've been holding on to all of it hoping someone will come to collect them.

42
04:17.674 --> 04:20.886
Maybe that's why you're here?

43
04:23.138 --> 04:27.851
[in Korean] No, just curious because you said he was Korean. Hmm.

44
04:33.940 --> 04:35.358
[in English] They always worked together.

45
04:36.193 --> 04:39.738
Researching different ways to successfully grow crops here.

46
04:40.864 --> 04:42.157
[♪ gentle music playing]

47
04:55.086 --> 04:57.172
How many photos are you going to take?

48
04:57.255 --> 04:58.548
They're so cute, aren't they?

49
04:58.632 --> 04:59.925
[shutter clicks]

50
05:00.008 --> 05:02.302
Every day you're snapping away.

51
05:02.385 --> 05:03.887
How are you not tired of that yet?

52
05:03.970 --> 05:05.096
[chuckles]

53
05:05.639 --> 05:07.182
Watching them grow brings me joy.

54
05:08.099 --> 05:10.143
Like how watching Karin grow makes you happy.

55
05:10.644 --> 05:11.645
It's sort of similar.

56
05:11.728 --> 05:13.063
[chuckling] Oh.

57
05:13.814 --> 05:14.940
Karin.

58
05:18.568 --> 05:20.403
Someday my son might come visit.

59
05:21.530 --> 05:24.658
Will you take care of this one so that he can see it?

60
05:25.242 --> 05:27.327
Yes, sir. Thanks for trusting me.

61
05:31.915 --> 05:33.333
[Karin] He was so kind.

62
05:33.416 --> 05:35.043
And he smiled a lot.

63
05:44.135 --> 05:45.178
[watch chimes]

64
05:48.932 --> 05:51.434
Well, I need to go to bed.

65
05:51.518 --> 05:52.519
[in Korean] Oh, right.

66
05:54.145 --> 05:56.147
I'll clean up in here before I go.

67
05:58.775 --> 06:00.694
-[in English] Sleep well, all right? -[in Korean] Yeah.

68
06:08.118 --> 06:09.494
[sighs]

69
06:24.759 --> 06:26.094
GENERAL PRINCIPLES OF SOIL AND FERTILIZERS

70
06:26.177 --> 06:28.054
[♪ melancholy music playing]

71
06:42.777 --> 06:44.321
[Gyeongsu, in Korean] New shoots sprouted today.

72
06:45.155 --> 06:47.532
How cold and hard it must've been beneath the soil.

73
06:48.533 --> 06:50.869
It's amazing how they were able to break through it.

74
06:52.287 --> 06:55.915
It somewhat reminded me of the day Yubin started school.

75
06:57.626 --> 07:00.879
I kept looking back at him in front of the school gates, watching him go in…

76
07:01.921 --> 07:03.131
Worried he might snap,

77
07:03.214 --> 07:05.342
like the sprouts that had just barely made it out of the soil…

78
07:06.843 --> 07:09.095
While these strawberries continue to rise toward me above the ground…

79
07:09.679 --> 07:12.891
Before I knew it, my son was growing up, leaving my arms.

80
07:13.892 --> 07:15.727
They're both thriving, and yet…

81
07:16.478 --> 07:18.104
It's a strange feeling.

82
07:21.399 --> 07:22.734
I think I miss him very much tonight.

83
07:45.840 --> 07:47.550
[in English] I better wake him up I guess.

84
08:16.538 --> 08:18.206
[♪ gentle music playing]

85
08:25.505 --> 08:26.756
Wow.

86
08:29.050 --> 08:30.885
He's got long lashes.

87
08:44.524 --> 08:46.568
[heartbeat thumping]

88
08:48.028 --> 08:49.404
-[heart rate monitor beeps] -[gasps]

89
08:50.447 --> 08:54.159
Oh, uh… The alarm… I forgot to turn it off, uh…

90
09:00.707 --> 09:02.125
Huh? [groans]

91
09:02.208 --> 09:03.668
[grunts]

92
09:03.752 --> 09:06.212
-[panting] -[beeping stops]

93
09:07.756 --> 09:08.757
[sighs]

94
09:10.425 --> 09:12.302
Why is my heart pounding so hard?

95
09:13.970 --> 09:14.971
-[knocking on door] -[gasps]

96
09:15.055 --> 09:18.516
Uh… "Let's meet at the farm later."

97
09:21.061 --> 09:22.771
You don't have to come to work today.

98
09:23.730 --> 09:24.898
[in Korean] Why not?

99
09:25.398 --> 09:29.527
[in English] Uh, um, actually… We're having a village meeting today.

100
09:39.496 --> 09:42.373
[in Korean] He must have been close with all the villagers.

101
09:46.503 --> 09:47.670
[in English] "I'm coming with you."

102
09:50.340 --> 09:53.009
-Why is that? -Uh, I'm coming with you.

103
09:54.260 --> 09:56.387
-Why is that? -I'm coming with--

104
09:56.971 --> 10:00.391
Uh-huh. Uh… Um, why is that?

105
10:02.894 --> 10:04.854
-[villager 1] Mr. Ikeda. -[villager 2] Oh, Mr. Ikeda.

106
10:04.938 --> 10:06.815
-I'm so glad you're here. -Hello there! Nice to see you.

107
10:06.898 --> 10:07.899
-Come on. -Let's go in.

108
10:07.982 --> 10:09.067
NEIGHBORHOOD COMMUNITY CENTER

109
10:09.776 --> 10:12.112
[villagers chattering]

110
10:17.784 --> 10:20.703
-Well, look who the cat dragged in. -[villagers] Hmm?

111
10:21.538 --> 10:22.705
This guy.

112
10:22.789 --> 10:25.542
He's a new employee who started working for Karin.

113
10:26.626 --> 10:27.669
[♪ tense music playing]

114
10:36.302 --> 10:39.264
-Uh… -Come in. Say hi to everyone.

115
10:43.184 --> 10:46.187
Uh… Uh…

116
10:46.271 --> 10:47.397
[in Korean] Hi.

117
10:47.981 --> 10:49.732
[in English] Go-Good morning.

118
10:50.233 --> 10:52.068
-[chuckles] I'm Yubin. -[villagers] Good morning.

119
10:52.152 --> 10:54.487
-[chuckles] -Good morning.

120
10:54.571 --> 10:55.572
[Yubin] Morning.

121
10:55.655 --> 10:56.865
[♪ entertaining music playing]

122
10:56.948 --> 10:58.158
[villagers murmuring]

123
11:07.083 --> 11:09.544
Ah, so he's Karin's new helper.

124
11:09.627 --> 11:13.298
He's got quite a body, and he's nice to look at.

125
11:13.381 --> 11:14.841
-Hey. -That's inappropriate.

126
11:14.924 --> 11:17.385
I bet you that he won't last here very long.

127
11:18.011 --> 11:22.974
He needs to have dedication too. It takes much more than a sturdy body, doesn't it?

128
11:23.057 --> 11:24.100
Mm-hmm.

129
11:24.184 --> 11:25.393
[in Korean] Hello there. Hi.

130
11:28.229 --> 11:31.024
-[in English] Good morning, everyone! -[villagers] Good morning.

131
11:31.107 --> 11:33.526
Let's all get this meeting started, shall we?

132
11:37.655 --> 11:38.781
Good news.

133
11:38.865 --> 11:42.702
Green Nova Corporation Festa will be held again this year!

134
11:45.914 --> 11:49.459
We have another wonderful opportunity to be part of the Festa,

135
11:49.542 --> 11:51.294
thanks to every one of you here.

136
11:52.086 --> 11:54.297
Everyone, uh, has a handout, right?

137
11:55.173 --> 11:58.009
The agenda for this meeting is on the first page.

138
11:58.092 --> 12:00.428
-[in Korean] What's Green Nova Festa? -Ah.

139
12:01.596 --> 12:04.599
It's a pretty big event where we get to promote our produce.

140
12:05.433 --> 12:08.394
It's held by the biggest agricultural company in all of Japan.

141
12:08.895 --> 12:12.523
Every region brings their signature produce to compete and sell.

142
12:13.983 --> 12:16.527
This year, it's going to be Karin whose crops will be evaluated.

143
12:18.446 --> 12:19.864
-Ah. -[in English] All right.

144
12:19.948 --> 12:21.741
Together there are four candidates.

145
12:21.824 --> 12:24.786
The first candidate is "Karin's Strawberries."

146
12:25.620 --> 12:28.164
-My farm's strengths are that… -[Kunam, in Korean] Isn't she amazing?

147
12:28.248 --> 12:30.792
[in English] …the strawberries can be grown in large quantities,

148
12:30.875 --> 12:32.293
and they're great quality.

149
12:32.377 --> 12:34.420
So I really hope you all are pleased.

150
12:34.504 --> 12:35.588
[Kunam, in Korean] Wow.

151
12:35.672 --> 12:38.883
How does Mari make turning pages look so chic?

152
12:38.967 --> 12:42.845
[Karin, in English] …and created a whole presentation, including drawings.

153
12:44.013 --> 12:47.767
Next up are the sweet potatoes we proudly showcase every year.

154
12:47.850 --> 12:50.186
We've been consistent on the amount we produce,

155
12:50.270 --> 12:53.815
so I'm pretty sure we'll be able to showcase them again.

156
12:53.898 --> 12:56.192
Advertising them will be very important.

157
12:56.276 --> 12:57.860
-[villager] Uh… -Yes, please go ahead.

158
12:59.195 --> 13:00.530
It's good to remember…

159
13:00.613 --> 13:02.657
That way we can make it a little more special…

160
13:05.868 --> 13:09.330
All right, why don't we continue this conversation outside while we eat.

161
13:09.414 --> 13:11.541
[villagers clamoring]

162
13:11.624 --> 13:12.750
Time for lunch.

163
13:13.584 --> 13:14.961
[Kunam, in Korean] We're going to eat first.

164
13:15.044 --> 13:17.380
Eat first? Oh, okay.

165
13:20.174 --> 13:21.509
-[in English] It's yummy, right? -So hungry.

166
13:21.592 --> 13:23.386
-Tell me when. Okay. -That's enough.

167
13:23.469 --> 13:24.595
This looks refreshing.

168
13:24.679 --> 13:26.306
This works out great.

169
13:27.307 --> 13:28.933
[villagers laughing]

170
13:29.017 --> 13:31.102
He's so handsome. Look at him.

171
13:31.686 --> 13:32.895
[chuckling]

172
13:37.984 --> 13:41.821
Kunam, Mari. Thanks for being our Festa cheering squad.

173
13:41.904 --> 13:43.406
Of course. Happy to help.

174
13:43.990 --> 13:47.827
I'm perfect. These guns, nice smile, and cute.

175
13:48.411 --> 13:49.787
I'll charm them all.

176
13:49.871 --> 13:51.164
You can count on me.

177
13:52.498 --> 13:53.750
Yeah!

178
13:53.833 --> 13:55.793
-[villager 1] You've got this! -[villager 2] Go, Kunam!

179
13:55.877 --> 13:58.463
[Mari] Why me? Why am I paired with Kunam?

180
13:59.088 --> 14:01.591
'Cause I mean, what about…

181
14:04.469 --> 14:08.473
Our Kunam is so cute and charming, but…

182
14:09.307 --> 14:12.185
Yeah, but this year's Festa is very…

183
14:12.727 --> 14:14.687
Very important for us.

184
14:17.523 --> 14:19.942
[whispers, speaks Korean] Hey, come here a minute.

185
14:23.071 --> 14:27.283
Why is everyone staring at me?

186
14:27.366 --> 14:29.452
[chief, in English] Hey, Kunam! What did he say?

187
14:32.663 --> 14:33.664
[in Korean] You see that?

188
14:34.665 --> 14:35.792
Right, my company went bust. So what?

189
14:35.875 --> 14:38.795
[Yubin] What? Why is he angry?

190
14:38.878 --> 14:40.838
[in English] He… He can't do it.

191
14:40.922 --> 14:42.006
-[both gasp] -[villager] Oh.

192
14:43.299 --> 14:48.221
Yubin is really famous in Korea, but he made mistakes.

193
14:48.304 --> 14:53.810
So he has to lay low here for a while. Uh, he has to avoid the loan sharks.

194
14:53.893 --> 14:55.061
[chuckles]

195
14:59.232 --> 15:01.484
-Oh, I knew he was trouble. -A troublemaker?

196
15:01.567 --> 15:03.027
See?

197
15:03.111 --> 15:08.449
[in Korean] What'd you tell them? Why are they all staring at me like that?

198
15:08.533 --> 15:10.118
[Kunam] Oh…

199
15:10.201 --> 15:12.537
They want your help with the designs for the Festa.

200
15:12.620 --> 15:14.622
You've done that a lot, right? Come on, man.

201
15:14.705 --> 15:17.667
How am I supposed to do designs for a rural event?

202
15:17.750 --> 15:19.210
I've never done anything like that before.

203
15:19.293 --> 15:23.005
This means everything to Karin.

204
15:23.589 --> 15:25.758
You said you had to make good with her.

205
15:26.551 --> 15:28.010
This is for Karin.

206
15:28.636 --> 15:29.637
[exclaims]

207
15:37.478 --> 15:41.566
Fine, fine. I'll do it.

208
15:41.649 --> 15:42.775
[chuckles]

209
15:43.860 --> 15:46.737
[in English] Instead, he'll be in charge of our designs!

210
15:46.821 --> 15:48.865
Give him a round of applause!

211
15:49.740 --> 15:51.284
[♪ joyful music playing]

212
15:54.162 --> 15:57.039
-Oh, what a sweet man. -Oh! So nice.

213
15:57.123 --> 15:59.041
[Yubin stuttering]

214
15:59.834 --> 16:01.460
[in English] Thank you very much. Thank you.

215
16:02.170 --> 16:03.713
[chief] Eat up and do your best.

216
16:03.796 --> 16:05.840
-Come on. Now eat. -You must be hungry.

217
16:05.923 --> 16:08.050
-Is it good? -[villager] Come by our shop any time.

218
16:08.134 --> 16:09.135
[chuckling]

219
16:09.635 --> 16:10.761
[Yubin] Thank you.

220
16:12.555 --> 16:14.849
-[villager] Is it good? -Hmm?

221
16:16.309 --> 16:17.393
Hmm?

222
16:19.395 --> 16:21.022
Thank you so much.

223
16:22.356 --> 16:23.649
Bye-bye.

224
16:32.033 --> 16:36.704
Kunam mentioned that you were really famous in Korea.

225
16:38.164 --> 16:39.749
What brought you here?

226
16:41.459 --> 16:44.045
[in Korean] Ah. I'm just buying some prop…

227
16:46.547 --> 16:47.548
What I meant was…

228
16:50.009 --> 16:52.720
I've got a lot going on in Korea. I just wanted to take a little break,

229
16:52.803 --> 16:53.804
but…

230
16:55.473 --> 16:57.516
I really like it here.

231
16:58.517 --> 16:59.644
It's so relaxing.

232
17:03.606 --> 17:04.607
[in English] I see.

233
17:05.691 --> 17:08.778
Anyway, thank you for volunteering.

234
17:09.654 --> 17:13.616
This Festa will make or break us.

235
17:15.952 --> 17:18.412
You can't tell from looking at them…

236
17:20.873 --> 17:24.085
but everyone's worried about me doing farm work alone.

237
17:26.045 --> 17:30.967
That's why this Festa's important. If my strawberries get recognition,

238
17:31.801 --> 17:33.970
they'll realize I'm capable on my own,

239
17:34.470 --> 17:36.180
and they'll be able to relax.

240
17:39.141 --> 17:41.310
[in Korean] This is a pretty huge deal, huh?

241
17:41.394 --> 17:43.229
[in English] Mm-hmm. Totally.

242
17:44.438 --> 17:46.941
-[in Korean] In that case… -Hmm?

243
17:47.984 --> 17:50.861
Since I'm helping you, could you do me a favor?

244
17:54.532 --> 17:55.992
[in English] What is it?

245
17:56.075 --> 17:57.618
[in Korean] Oh, please just let me sleep in here!

246
17:57.702 --> 18:00.830
[in English] Absolutely not. We are not sleeping together in the same space.

247
18:00.913 --> 18:01.914
[in Korean] Come on!

248
18:01.998 --> 18:03.207
-[in English] Stop it! -Why "stop it," huh?

249
18:03.291 --> 18:04.625
Why "stop it"? No "stop it," no "stop it."

250
18:04.709 --> 18:06.877
-No way! -You said you'd do whatever I want!

251
18:06.961 --> 18:08.879
-[in English] Why, "Stop it"? Tell me why! -I said no!

252
18:08.963 --> 18:11.841
[in Korean] Remember when I got drenched last time?

253
18:11.924 --> 18:13.926
I can't stay there!

254
18:14.010 --> 18:15.845
It gets so cold and hot.

255
18:15.928 --> 18:21.100
No matter how much I sweep, there's always more dust!

256
18:21.183 --> 18:23.811
I'm allergic to dust.

257
18:23.894 --> 18:26.939
I'm just not going to last if I keep on staying in that dump.

258
18:27.023 --> 18:29.775
For me, for you, and for the strawberries.

259
18:29.859 --> 18:33.696
We need to keep brainstorming together so we can win first place in this Festa.

260
18:33.779 --> 18:35.615
[in English] All right! Okay, listen!

261
18:35.698 --> 18:36.699
It's fine.

262
18:38.826 --> 18:40.161
-I'll allow it. -Huh?

263
18:40.244 --> 18:42.913
But if you break any of the rules, you are out of here.

264
18:42.997 --> 18:44.081
-Ru-rules? Rules? -Rules.

265
18:44.165 --> 18:45.499
Oh? O-Okay. Rules.

266
18:45.583 --> 18:49.503
[in Korean] Okay, I'll sleep right here. Okay? Okay, great.

267
18:49.587 --> 18:51.964
-[in English] Rules? Okay. Rules are good. -Rules.

268
18:52.048 --> 18:53.758
Rules I really really like.

269
18:56.594 --> 18:58.346
[in Korean] There are so many.

270
18:58.429 --> 19:00.431
But I can't read any of this.

271
19:03.309 --> 19:04.810
[in English] Rule number one.

272
19:04.894 --> 19:08.230
You are not to come out to the living room after 11:00 p.m.

273
19:15.446 --> 19:19.283
In particular, sleeping on that sofa from now on is off limits.

274
19:21.160 --> 19:22.161
[in Korean] What is this, prison?

275
19:22.244 --> 19:23.245
[in English] Secondly.

276
19:23.329 --> 19:25.456
At all times you are to be properly dressed.

277
19:25.539 --> 19:27.083
[in Korean] Even though it's indoors?

278
19:27.166 --> 19:28.459
[in English] The third rule is,

279
19:28.542 --> 19:30.127
that my room is off-limits.

280
19:33.255 --> 19:35.132
[in Korean] I don't even want to go in your room.

281
19:35.883 --> 19:39.470
[sighs, speaks English] You can read the rest of the rules on your own time.

282
19:40.846 --> 19:42.264
4. YUBIN IN CHARGE OF TAKING OUT ALL THE TRASH.

283
19:42.348 --> 19:43.891
5. YUBIN ALSO IN CHARGE OF CLEANING ALL WATER AREAS

284
19:43.974 --> 19:45.893
6. KEEP SHARED AREAS CLEAN

285
19:46.477 --> 19:49.355
Oh, and finally, we'll eat our breakfast together.

286
19:49.438 --> 19:51.774
[in Korean] You'll make breakfast for me?

287
19:52.358 --> 19:54.360
[sighs, speaks English] You'll be making our breakfast.

288
19:54.443 --> 19:55.945
So we can save money on food.

289
19:56.028 --> 19:59.448
[in Korean] This is straight-up unfair.

290
20:00.241 --> 20:02.868
[in English] Don't forget that breaking the rules gets you kicked out.

291
20:05.538 --> 20:07.498
[♪ comical music playing]

292
20:13.671 --> 20:14.672
Ah, r-rules?

293
20:14.755 --> 20:15.923
-Mm-hmm. -Mmm.

294
20:16.006 --> 20:17.925
Rules, I-I like it.

295
20:21.762 --> 20:22.763
[sighs]

296
20:27.309 --> 20:28.436
[sighs]

297
20:30.479 --> 20:31.731
What the heck?

298
20:34.066 --> 20:35.401
Did I miss my dose?

299
20:35.484 --> 20:36.944
No, I'm sure I took it.

300
20:38.863 --> 20:40.698
Is it because I should be asleep?

301
20:45.870 --> 20:47.037
[sighs]

302
20:47.621 --> 20:48.706
Oh, whatever!

303
20:49.582 --> 20:51.083
[sighs]

304
20:51.667 --> 20:52.668
[whines]

305
20:53.210 --> 20:54.795
[grunts]

306
20:54.879 --> 20:56.297
What is going on?

307
20:57.965 --> 20:59.091
[grunts]

308
20:59.175 --> 21:01.010
[cicadas croak]

309
21:05.598 --> 21:07.266
[♪ upbeat music playing]

310
21:18.486 --> 21:19.570
Hey, move.

311
21:19.653 --> 21:20.905
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

312
21:22.281 --> 21:23.699
Oh.

313
21:27.328 --> 21:28.329
-My bad. -Uh…

314
21:28.996 --> 21:31.499
[Karin] Chopsticks go in the front.

315
21:32.291 --> 21:35.169
-[in Korean] Huh? Ah. Ah. [grunts] -[in English] Here.

316
21:35.753 --> 21:37.171
[in Korean] That's not it.

317
21:37.254 --> 21:38.255
[in English] Put them here.

318
21:38.339 --> 21:40.090
[Karin] Wait, what? No, no, no.

319
21:40.174 --> 21:43.260
-That's wrong. Hey, no, in front of you. -[in Korean] That's the correct way.

320
21:43.344 --> 21:44.845
-No, like this. -[in English] You're wrong.

321
21:44.929 --> 21:46.222
They go in front.

322
21:46.305 --> 21:47.515
[in Korean] Okay, okay. I get it.

323
21:48.140 --> 21:50.643
-[in English] Okay. So mine go here. -Mm-hmm.

324
21:51.685 --> 21:53.729
[Yubin] And yours go there.

325
21:53.813 --> 21:55.815
-Go right here. Okay. -Yeah. Okay.

326
21:57.316 --> 21:58.484
[both] Thanks for the meal.

327
21:58.567 --> 22:00.736
PRAYING FOR VICTORY

328
22:00.820 --> 22:03.739
SHOP FOR SUPPLIES

329
22:03.823 --> 22:05.783
-We need a rope. -Hmm? A rope?

330
22:05.866 --> 22:07.159
-And clips. -Clips?

331
22:07.243 --> 22:09.703
-Okay, and then what else? -Then?

332
22:25.803 --> 22:27.638
That's pretty. [chuckles]

333
22:40.359 --> 22:41.986
-Karin. -Mmm?

334
22:42.069 --> 22:43.362
What is your favorite color?

335
22:43.445 --> 22:45.447
-My favorite? It's red. -Mmm.

336
22:45.531 --> 22:46.782
-Huh? -This color.

337
22:46.866 --> 22:48.868
-Oh, that's red. Ah. -Mm-hmm.

338
22:51.871 --> 22:54.248
-No. No, you can't see. -What?

339
22:54.331 --> 22:56.959
-[in Korean] You don't get to see it. -[in English] How come I can't? Why not?

340
22:57.042 --> 22:58.168
Mmm.

341
23:00.004 --> 23:02.673
-Hey. -Why can't I see it?

342
23:02.756 --> 23:04.633
[in Korean] You can't read Korean anyway.

343
23:04.717 --> 23:06.385
-Huh? -Here, look at it.

344
23:06.468 --> 23:07.469
-Plushies. -Aw.

345
23:07.553 --> 23:09.680
-[in English] Look how cute these are. -Oh! Pig?

346
23:09.763 --> 23:11.056
-Pig. Pig. -Pig? You pig?

347
23:11.140 --> 23:12.975
-You pig? [chuckles] -I am not a pig.

348
23:13.058 --> 23:14.226
What the heck?

349
23:14.310 --> 23:17.021
-[in Korean] This one looks like you. -Mm-hmm.

350
23:17.104 --> 23:18.397
[in English] Looks like you.

351
23:18.480 --> 23:20.649
-Like me? Really? You think? -Uh-huh.

352
23:20.733 --> 23:22.651
[laughing] Aw, cute.

353
23:23.527 --> 23:25.154
-[mutters] -Are you two newlyweds?

354
23:25.779 --> 23:26.864
What?

355
23:27.448 --> 23:29.366
Ah, we're, uh, not together. [chuckles]

356
23:29.450 --> 23:30.826
-Take your time. -[mutters]

357
23:30.910 --> 23:32.369
Oh, thank you.

358
23:33.078 --> 23:34.747
[sighs] Let's go. [chuckles]

359
23:34.830 --> 23:36.206
Uh, Ka--

360
23:37.875 --> 23:40.127
Karin. Karin. Karin!

361
23:41.754 --> 23:44.131
-That's all we need, right? Done shopping. -Mm-hmm.

362
23:44.214 --> 23:47.134
Wow, your Japanese has improved a lot.

363
23:47.968 --> 23:49.637
I'm a Japanese learning genius.

364
23:49.720 --> 23:51.513
-Uh-huh, you are. [laughs] -Yeah. [chuckles]

365
23:51.597 --> 23:53.682
-So good. So good. -So good.

366
23:54.558 --> 23:56.435
Whoa, is that Sleepyhead?

367
23:59.521 --> 24:02.358
Hey, Reiji, stop wandering away from us.

368
24:02.441 --> 24:03.984
Next time wait for us, please.

369
24:04.068 --> 24:05.694
You're too close. Stand over there.

370
24:06.278 --> 24:07.696
Yay, great.

371
24:07.780 --> 24:10.699
Hey, it must be fate that I ran into you here.

372
24:10.783 --> 24:12.117
Why are you here?

373
24:12.201 --> 24:14.244
I came back for the Festa. Why else?

374
24:15.704 --> 24:17.748
I'm a three-time consecutive winner.

375
24:17.831 --> 24:19.166
Right.

376
24:20.542 --> 24:23.629
Wait a sec, are you… gonna exhibit too?

377
24:23.712 --> 24:26.215
-Of course. -[sighs] Are you some kind of idiot?

378
24:26.298 --> 24:29.259
You might as well give up now, because you're not gonna make it.

379
24:30.928 --> 24:33.138
I'm sweeping the comps again this year.

380
24:33.973 --> 24:34.974
You should just chill.

381
24:36.517 --> 24:37.559
[sighs]

382
24:37.643 --> 24:40.229
Well, see you at the Festa, Sleepyhead.

383
24:41.480 --> 24:42.648
Whoa.

384
24:46.276 --> 24:47.277
You're a hottie.

385
24:47.778 --> 24:49.029
Hot guy.

386
24:55.786 --> 24:56.954
-Hmm. -Hmm.

387
25:15.180 --> 25:16.181
[chuckles]

388
25:17.850 --> 25:20.060
-It's hot. -Thank you.

389
25:32.865 --> 25:34.116
Hmm.

390
25:35.743 --> 25:37.494
[in Korean] Who was that guy earlier?

391
25:37.578 --> 25:38.579
[stammers]

392
25:39.329 --> 25:41.665
That really smug-looking guy?

393
25:46.545 --> 25:48.130
[in English] We went to college together.

394
25:49.131 --> 25:50.883
He's a real jerk.

395
25:50.966 --> 25:53.427
But he's also a three-time Festa winner.

396
25:56.263 --> 25:57.264
Ah.

397
25:57.973 --> 25:58.974
"Sleepyhead"?

398
26:00.309 --> 26:03.145
"Sleepyhead." [in Korean] What is that, like, your nickname?

399
26:05.856 --> 26:07.024
Mm-hmm.

400
26:17.701 --> 26:19.870
-[in English] Aren't you cold? -Oh, uh…

401
26:19.953 --> 26:21.789
It's not that cold actually.

402
26:22.456 --> 26:23.707
I'm feeling toasty.

403
26:29.088 --> 26:30.756
Should we hold hands?

404
26:32.424 --> 26:33.425
Huh?

405
26:38.305 --> 26:41.308
[heartbeat thumping]

406
26:45.979 --> 26:48.357
-[friend] Karin? Karin, Karin! -[body thuds]

407
26:48.440 --> 26:49.650
[murmuring]

408
26:49.733 --> 26:51.902
[friend] Karin, Karin.

409
26:53.195 --> 26:55.823
Karin! Karin! Karin!

410
26:55.906 --> 26:57.157
W-Will you watch her?

411
26:57.241 --> 26:58.575
I-I'm gonna go get help.

412
27:03.789 --> 27:05.415
[student] Should we call an ambulance?

413
27:11.630 --> 27:13.715
[student 1] He just left her lying there and ran off.

414
27:13.799 --> 27:16.385
[student 2 scoffs] She passed out holding hands?

415
27:16.468 --> 27:18.345
What if he kissed her? [laughs]

416
27:18.428 --> 27:20.472
[student 3] She could die if you touch her.

417
27:24.226 --> 27:26.979
Hey, Reiji. Don't you have a major crush on Karin?

418
27:27.062 --> 27:28.564
[Reiji] What? No way.

419
27:29.064 --> 27:33.277
Are you an idiot? Why would I be interested in that sleepyhead? Come on.

420
27:33.360 --> 27:35.112
[students laughing]

421
27:37.197 --> 27:40.075
[student 4] She's a sleeping love fairy. [laughing]

422
27:40.158 --> 27:44.746
[Karin] I was teased for a long time all because of him.

423
27:48.792 --> 27:52.921
When I'm stressed out or when my emotions get too intense,

424
27:53.005 --> 27:55.757
my nervous system gets all out of whack.

425
27:56.300 --> 27:58.594
It's like a switch shutting my body down.

426
27:59.803 --> 28:00.804
Switch, huh?

427
28:01.430 --> 28:02.472
Mm-hmm.

428
28:03.891 --> 28:06.018
I short circuit like some kind of robot.

429
28:07.603 --> 28:08.770
I just pass out.

430
28:11.481 --> 28:13.358
[heart rate monitor beeping]

431
28:14.192 --> 28:15.277
[gasps]

432
28:16.403 --> 28:17.404
[beeping stops]

433
28:23.911 --> 28:26.330
[chuckles] But what I've decided…

434
28:28.081 --> 28:31.543
is that it's better to think of it as a star falling.

435
28:32.669 --> 28:35.339
A star falling?

436
28:35.422 --> 28:36.506
Mm-hmm.

437
28:37.841 --> 28:41.178
It's like my heart shines so brightly that it had to…

438
28:42.387 --> 28:44.556
go dark and rest for a little while.

439
28:47.184 --> 28:50.395
And when I wake up, it's magically recharged.

440
29:01.073 --> 29:03.700
[in Korean] I'm making sure you take first place.

441
29:05.953 --> 29:06.954
Hmm?

442
29:07.663 --> 29:09.122
[in English] Just trust me.

443
29:10.999 --> 29:13.126
-[chuckles] -[laughs]

444
29:13.794 --> 29:15.379
-What? -Just trust me.

445
29:15.462 --> 29:17.297
-Trust you with what? -Mmm.

446
29:17.798 --> 29:20.050
[laughs]

447
29:20.133 --> 29:21.134
Hmm.

448
29:21.802 --> 29:24.972
Karin, I am your worker.

449
29:25.472 --> 29:26.640
Put your trust in me.

450
29:27.849 --> 29:30.686
-We're gonna win! [cheers] -[cheers, laughs]

451
29:30.769 --> 29:31.853
[both chuckling]

452
29:42.698 --> 29:44.950
[♪ upbeat, quirky music playing]

453
29:49.788 --> 29:51.289
PRAYING FOR VICTORY BUY NECESSARY SUPPLIES

454
29:51.373 --> 29:52.374
CHEER SQUAD PRACTICE

455
30:11.852 --> 30:13.687
You sure that's the routine you wanna do?

456
30:14.396 --> 30:15.397
Mm-hmm.

457
30:15.480 --> 30:18.483
I wanna make sure that the Festa win goes to Charo Island.

458
30:19.276 --> 30:22.195
That way, Charo will gain recognition,

459
30:22.279 --> 30:24.740
and Karin's strawberries will get the support they need.

460
30:25.907 --> 30:27.200
Besides…

461
30:28.160 --> 30:31.288
A winning prize for Charo will make you happy, Mari.

462
30:31.371 --> 30:32.914
[gasps]

463
30:39.755 --> 30:41.381
Hmm. Yeah?

464
30:41.965 --> 30:45.385
Then I guess I should help you help our island.

465
30:45.469 --> 30:47.137
-You serious? -Mm-hmm.

466
30:48.764 --> 30:50.932
-[Mari laughs] -[straining]

467
30:51.016 --> 30:55.020
The cheer squad is working really hard in preparation for the Festa.

468
30:55.103 --> 30:56.396
How will Kunam…

469
30:56.480 --> 30:57.481
BUILD STAMINA

470
30:57.564 --> 31:00.442
…our courageous cheer squad leader, lead Charo Island to victory?

471
31:01.902 --> 31:02.903
[Kunam grunts]

472
31:02.986 --> 31:04.529
[Mari] Is that heavy, Kunam?

473
31:05.197 --> 31:08.158
Oh. This is nothing.

474
31:08.241 --> 31:09.951
-I got this. -[laughs]

475
31:10.035 --> 31:12.871
Then pick up the pace. Go, go!

476
31:13.455 --> 31:18.627
But what does the cheer training have to do with dragging this tire?

477
31:18.710 --> 31:21.296
Cheerleading takes a lot of stamina, you know.

478
31:21.379 --> 31:22.839
[pants]

479
31:22.923 --> 31:26.343
Hey, come back here! You can't ditch!

480
31:26.426 --> 31:28.386
-I can't do it. -You can.

481
31:28.470 --> 31:30.514
-One more lap. -I can't, I can't. No way.

482
31:30.597 --> 31:32.265
-Okay! Oh! I can't do it! -Yes, you can! You can!

483
31:32.349 --> 31:34.726
-Come on! [screams] -[laughs]

484
31:34.810 --> 31:36.394
-Wait! Hey! -[both laugh]

485
31:36.978 --> 31:39.064
Never say never. Just one more try.

486
31:39.147 --> 31:41.525
-You're not done yet. Let' go! -That's it.

487
31:42.484 --> 31:45.237
Kunam! Wait, hey, hang on!

488
31:46.113 --> 31:47.322
-Hey, wait! -Run away?

489
31:47.405 --> 31:48.406
-Wait for me! -Okay!

490
31:48.990 --> 31:50.325
[Mari] Caught you!

491
31:52.369 --> 31:53.370
Hi!

492
31:54.287 --> 31:55.288
Nice to see you.

493
31:56.081 --> 31:57.124
[in Korean] I see.

494
31:57.958 --> 31:59.626
CHARO ISLAND

495
31:59.709 --> 32:00.836
[in English] We're here.

496
32:01.419 --> 32:03.713
Oh. What?

497
32:04.881 --> 32:06.216
-We're here? -Mmm. Right here.

498
32:06.299 --> 32:08.009
-Charo Island, here? -Yeah.

499
32:08.635 --> 32:09.636
Like it?

500
32:09.719 --> 32:10.846
[in Korean] Wow, this is…

501
32:12.055 --> 32:13.306
Uh, Karin.

502
32:13.807 --> 32:15.183
-Mm-hmm? -Uh…

503
32:15.809 --> 32:18.228
This spot, right here? It's good.

504
32:18.311 --> 32:19.896
-Not bad at all. -[in English] It's good?

505
32:20.522 --> 32:21.648
-You like it! -Hmm.

506
32:21.731 --> 32:23.859
The spot is always picked by lottery.

507
32:23.942 --> 32:26.486
And I have a lucky streak of winning those.

508
32:26.570 --> 32:28.113
Mmm. Mmm.

509
32:28.613 --> 32:31.449
-[chuckles] -Nice. Well done.

510
32:31.533 --> 32:33.285
-[Karin laughs] -Good work.

511
32:35.162 --> 32:38.290
[in Korean] All right, so now… [sighs] Uh…

512
32:38.790 --> 32:40.000
Okay.

513
32:41.042 --> 32:47.924
[murmuring] From here, and then like this here…

514
32:49.426 --> 32:51.678
[continues murmuring]

515
32:52.512 --> 32:54.639
[♪ gentle music playing]

516
32:57.767 --> 32:59.603
The staff will then…

517
33:09.654 --> 33:11.239
Okay. I got it.

518
33:14.576 --> 33:19.122
What's your main goal at this Festa?

519
33:19.706 --> 33:20.957
-[in English] My goal? -Mmm.

520
33:22.375 --> 33:23.460
Hmm.

521
33:24.044 --> 33:25.045
I…

522
33:25.629 --> 33:26.838
Hmm.

523
33:30.050 --> 33:31.968
It's not a huge one,

524
33:32.052 --> 33:35.055
but I want everybody to feel the spirit of Charo Island.

525
33:37.349 --> 33:38.725
-[in Korean] Get the feel of it? -Mm-hmm.

526
33:38.808 --> 33:40.977
[in English] I want to share the warmth and sincerity

527
33:41.061 --> 33:42.979
of both our village and its people.

528
33:44.064 --> 33:47.901
Along with, winning our village the grand prize.

529
33:53.615 --> 33:57.202
That one might be a pipe dream, I guess.

530
33:57.994 --> 34:00.538
We put our best foot forward every year, but…

531
34:01.623 --> 34:05.168
but, uh, we just never win.

532
34:05.835 --> 34:06.836
[chuckles]

533
34:08.463 --> 34:09.464
[chuckles]

534
34:11.841 --> 34:14.594
-Karin, you know… -Hmm?

535
34:14.678 --> 34:17.264
-…I studied Japanese yesterday. -Mm-hmm.

536
34:17.347 --> 34:18.682
[in Korean] Oh. Wait a minute.

537
34:18.765 --> 34:20.267
-[in English] Wait a minute. Mmm… -Hmm.

538
34:21.059 --> 34:23.353
[in Korean] So what I practiced yesterday is…

539
34:24.020 --> 34:25.188
Uh…

540
34:26.022 --> 34:27.023
Ah, here it is.

541
34:28.191 --> 34:30.026
[in English] "Fall seven times, stand up eight."

542
34:31.111 --> 34:32.112
What?

543
34:32.946 --> 34:35.907
Where on earth did you learn that phrase from, Yubin?

544
34:35.991 --> 34:37.826
Uh… I learned from Asahi.

545
34:38.410 --> 34:39.661
-Grandpa Asahi… -Uh-huh. Yeah.

546
34:39.744 --> 34:41.997
-…taught me… He said, uh… -Uh-huh. Okay.

547
34:42.080 --> 34:43.164
He-He taught me that.

548
34:43.248 --> 34:45.625
-Oh. Grandpa Asahi did? -Yeah. Mm-hmm.

549
34:45.709 --> 34:49.629
I am moneyless. That means my money is gone, yes?

550
34:49.713 --> 34:50.922
-[in Korean] I got scammed. -Uh-huh.

551
34:51.006 --> 34:52.215
-[in English] Scammed, yeah. -Uh-huh.

552
34:52.299 --> 34:54.009
He told me, "Fall seven times,

553
34:54.092 --> 34:55.802
-stand up eight." -I see.

554
34:55.885 --> 34:57.220
[both laugh]

555
34:57.304 --> 34:58.346
Stand up eight.

556
34:59.055 --> 35:00.849
Mmm. You're right.

557
35:01.474 --> 35:03.143
-Let's do our best. Mmm. -Mmm.

558
35:03.643 --> 35:05.312
[electronic beeping]

559
35:06.771 --> 35:08.690
[clock] Hello. [chirping]

560
35:08.773 --> 35:10.066
[groans]

561
35:10.775 --> 35:12.569
[groans]

562
35:12.652 --> 35:13.945
[grunts]

563
35:14.029 --> 35:15.697
-Ugh… -[chirping continues]

564
35:15.780 --> 35:17.115
[in Korean] How do I turn this thing off?

565
35:22.579 --> 35:24.331
-[in English] There. -Oh.

566
35:30.837 --> 35:33.381
-Hey, good morning. -Morning. [chuckles]

567
35:33.465 --> 35:35.508
PRAYING FOR VICTORY PREPARING CHARO ISLAND'S SOIL

568
35:35.592 --> 35:36.718
Hi there, Chief!

569
35:36.801 --> 35:39.346
-Sorry for the wait. -We need some soil.

570
35:40.221 --> 35:43.308
Wow! Oh! Nice!

571
35:44.392 --> 35:45.393
Very nice.

572
35:45.477 --> 35:46.478
It's perfect.

573
35:47.103 --> 35:48.313
Perfect.

574
35:50.482 --> 35:51.483
MAKING THE BOOTH DECORATIONS

575
35:51.566 --> 35:54.152
-[chattering] -Can you make sure it's right?

576
35:54.235 --> 35:57.197
-Take a look. Give it a spin. See that? -[exclaims]

577
35:57.906 --> 35:59.199
-I think it needs… -Mm-hmm.

578
35:59.282 --> 36:01.201
-…a little bit of tape. -Ah, okay.

579
36:01.785 --> 36:03.745
-[Karin] Hey, hold on. -Wait, wait.

580
36:03.828 --> 36:05.538
STRATEGY MEETING

581
36:05.622 --> 36:06.623
[Karin] What?

582
36:08.083 --> 36:10.418
-This one. -No, no, no. [in Korean] This one.

583
36:10.502 --> 36:12.962
-[in English] Why are you-- What? -[in Korean] Wait. Gosh, hold on.

584
36:13.046 --> 36:16.091
-It has to go that way. -[in English] No, it's this--

585
36:16.174 --> 36:19.511
No, the lights, they should go all around. Shoo!

586
36:19.594 --> 36:21.388
-Bam! -[in Korean] No, it's more like, wham!

587
36:21.471 --> 36:23.431
[in English] I'm in charge. Designer, designer.

588
36:23.515 --> 36:24.516
But I'm the leader.

589
36:26.017 --> 36:27.018
[in Korean] Rock, paper, scissors!

590
36:27.102 --> 36:28.436
-[laughs] -[in English] One more time.

591
36:28.520 --> 36:29.688
Best out of three. Ready?

592
36:39.781 --> 36:41.366
[♪ playful music playing]

593
36:46.204 --> 36:47.414
[Karin clears throat]

594
36:49.249 --> 36:51.543
Uh… Are you looking for something, Karin?

595
36:54.504 --> 36:55.505
Will this work?

596
36:56.047 --> 36:57.799
[in Korean] Oh. Thank you.

597
36:58.299 --> 36:59.300
All right then.

598
36:59.384 --> 37:00.802
-"Hello." -"Hello."

599
37:00.885 --> 37:03.096
-"Let's get to work." -"Let's get to work."

600
37:03.179 --> 37:05.098
-"This way." -"This way."

601
37:05.181 --> 37:07.183
-"It's okay." -"It's okay."

602
37:07.267 --> 37:10.520
"This way. That way. Together."

603
37:10.603 --> 37:13.898
[in English] You're learning this because of Yubin, right?

604
37:13.982 --> 37:18.653
No, I… No, the Festa. The Festa! We're prepping it together.

605
37:18.737 --> 37:21.030
The communication is a little difficult.

606
37:21.114 --> 37:22.323
I get it. That's great!

607
37:23.199 --> 37:24.784
Let's cheer each other on!

608
37:25.368 --> 37:27.328
Yeah, okay. Thanks a lot.

609
37:27.412 --> 37:29.330
[in Korean] Uh, th-thanks. Thanks.

610
37:29.414 --> 37:30.999
COMMUNICATION CLASS

611
37:33.835 --> 37:35.503
FINAL CHECKS

612
37:45.972 --> 37:49.726
[in English] This looks delicious! Thank you! Wow!

613
37:50.310 --> 37:51.352
Mmm…

614
37:56.858 --> 37:59.235
Hey, Chief, the inventory's complete.

615
37:59.319 --> 38:02.614
It would be a good idea for us to bring some extra strawberry jam along.

616
38:02.697 --> 38:03.698
[chief] Sounds good.

617
38:03.782 --> 38:07.035
As soon as we finish up here, we'll take everything out to the cars.

618
38:07.619 --> 38:09.287
Sounds like a plan. [chuckles]

619
38:11.998 --> 38:13.500
[phone buzzing]

620
38:20.006 --> 38:21.049
[in Korean] Look how pretty.

621
38:26.054 --> 38:27.764
[phone buzzes]

622
38:30.558 --> 38:32.644
[Karin, in English] Just like my strawberries, right?

623
38:33.186 --> 38:34.187
[chuckles]

624
38:37.982 --> 38:39.442
[Yubin] Great work today.

625
38:39.526 --> 38:41.152
[Karin] Great work to you too.

626
38:41.236 --> 38:42.821
[Yubin, in Korean] All right. [grunts]

627
38:44.906 --> 38:46.157
[strains]

628
38:46.241 --> 38:48.535
-Here. -[in English] Oh, sorry, but

629
38:48.618 --> 38:53.289
-drinking alcohol isn't for me. -[in Korean] Huh? Oh, I see.

630
38:53.957 --> 38:55.083
[in Korean] In that case…

631
38:55.166 --> 38:57.085
-[in English] Just a moment. -[exclaims]

632
38:58.253 --> 39:01.714
-I'll be right back. Wait. [chuckles] -Oh? Hmm?

633
39:11.349 --> 39:12.475
Huh?

634
39:13.518 --> 39:15.353
[in Korean] What's with the helmet?

635
39:15.436 --> 39:17.689
[in English] It's like my armor.

636
39:17.772 --> 39:20.483
-Just in case I faint or something. -Mmm.

637
39:21.734 --> 39:22.735
Okay.

638
39:23.820 --> 39:26.739
Whoo-hoo, it's been so long!

639
39:28.408 --> 39:29.659
-[in Korean] Cheers. -Cheers.

640
39:35.707 --> 39:37.542
-[both gasp] -Mmm.

641
39:38.042 --> 39:39.794
-Isn't it good? -Mm-hmm.

642
39:40.295 --> 39:42.714
[in English] It tastes amazing 'cause it's been a while.

643
39:42.797 --> 39:44.048
Mmm. [chuckles]

644
39:47.010 --> 39:48.136
[Karin sighs]

645
39:50.221 --> 39:51.347
[Yubin, in Korean] So, hey.

646
39:51.931 --> 39:56.394
Don't you get scared living here alone?

647
39:56.477 --> 39:58.479
[in English] I like living alone. You're more scary.

648
39:59.981 --> 40:00.982
Huh?

649
40:01.065 --> 40:02.901
[chuckles, speaks Korean] Come on, now.

650
40:02.984 --> 40:04.152
[chuckles]

651
40:08.489 --> 40:09.616
[in English] It's just that…

652
40:11.951 --> 40:15.830
I've always felt like a burden to every single person in my life.

653
40:18.499 --> 40:20.668
Everyone is always worrying because

654
40:21.711 --> 40:24.380
I could collapse anywhere at any second.

655
40:26.174 --> 40:27.842
It's always bothered me.

656
40:34.307 --> 40:39.020
That's why I've made it my mission to prove to the world

657
40:39.562 --> 40:41.356
that I can make it on my own.

658
40:42.690 --> 40:44.859
And I don't need anybody's help at all.

659
40:53.910 --> 40:55.703
[in Korean] It's okay to depend on others.

660
40:57.330 --> 40:58.331
There's no shame in that.

661
41:00.166 --> 41:01.376
Plus, you've got me.

662
41:02.126 --> 41:05.296
I'll catch you every time you faint.

663
41:05.380 --> 41:07.799
Like the first time we met.

664
41:08.967 --> 41:12.971
I'll hold you like this, okay?

665
41:13.054 --> 41:15.098
[scoffs, speaks English] When did I ever--

666
41:15.974 --> 41:16.975
[laughs]

667
41:20.436 --> 41:22.397
[in Korean] What I meant to say was…

668
41:24.983 --> 41:26.275
you don't need the helmet.

669
41:29.529 --> 41:30.738
Because with me,

670
41:32.573 --> 41:34.033
you don't have to be ashamed.

671
41:53.553 --> 41:54.804
[in English] I'll trust you, Yubin.

672
41:57.140 --> 41:59.100
[in Korean] You can trust me.

673
42:07.442 --> 42:08.443
[sighs]

674
42:23.374 --> 42:26.127
-[insects trilling] -[waves lapping]

675
42:50.443 --> 42:51.861
[sighs]

676
43:00.536 --> 43:01.537
[gasps]

677
43:02.914 --> 43:04.457
[♪ upbeat music playing]

678
43:16.010 --> 43:18.262
MERRY BERRY LOVE

679
43:18.346 --> 43:19.430
NEXT EPISODE

680
43:19.514 --> 43:21.599
[Karin, in English] The day's finally here.

681
43:21.682 --> 43:23.226
[Yubin] It's all right. Everything will work out.

682
43:23.309 --> 43:25.812
-[both sigh] -They are uncannily similar.

683
43:25.895 --> 43:29.524
[emcee] Green Nova Corporation Festa, the winner is…
